The upstream module picks the AES key by the position of a sample's description: the first uses
Apple's fixed prefetch key, the second the song's own key. That holds for the masters with audio
groups, whose stream playlists list both keys. A song Apple encoded only as AAC has a master
without audio groups: its stream playlists list the song's key alone, its file has one sample
description, and every sample is encrypted with the song's key. The caller now says which case it
is (it knows from the playlist), instead of the song's samples being decrypted with the fixed key.

